 To find the cross product, we use the determinant of a matrix with unit vectors $\hat{i}$, $\hat{j}$, $\hat{k}$ in the first row, the components of the first vector in the second row, and the components of the second vector in the third row. This gives us: \[
\begin{pmatrix} \hat{i} & \hat{j} & \hat{k} \\ 1 & -1 & 2 \\ 3 & 4 & -5 \end{pmatrix}
\] Expanding the determinant, we get: \[
\hat{i}((-1)(-5) - (2)(4)) - \hat{j}((1)(-5) - (2)(3)) + \hat{k}((1)(4) - (-1)(3)) = \hat{i}(5 - 8) - \hat{j}(-5 - 6) + \hat{k}(4 + 3) = -3\hat{i} + 11\hat{j} + 7\hat{k}
\] </think> <answer> $\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\ 11 \\ 7 \end{pmatrix}$ </answer>

